    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d405-a2">

                <pb facs="0433" n="427" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg427"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    72.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Moret to Mr. Taylor.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-11-24"><hi rendition="#small-caps">November</hi> 24,
                            1893</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Distinguished Sir and Friend</hi>: Pardon me if I
                    am not as yet able to fix a day for our interview upon the several pending
                    affairs.</p>
                <p>I will do so as soon as I can have the time; and I hope you will excuse me if, on
                    account of the urgency and gravity of the affairs which at present claim the
                    whole attention of the Government, I delay the discussion of those to be settled
                    with your legation, which certainly are not of small importance, but which are,
                    however, able to suffer that delay, for which I beg to apologize.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. Moret.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
